opentubex (0.37.0) stable; urgency=medium

  [ Highlights ]
  * Navigation, quick settings, player controls and fullscreen actions are now
    customized on one "Customize interface" page in Appearance settings, with a
    live preview of each. Its Control bar tab hides and reorders the player's
    control bar buttons
  * You can now hide AI slop channels with the community-maintained AiSList.
    Turn on "Hide AI slop channels" under Settings → Add-ons to hide listed
    channels from search results and recommendations and to tag videos from
    channels that likely post AI-generated content.
  * Added home screen widgets on Android and iOS. Continue watching resumes your
    latest unfinished videos where you left off, and Quick access opens Search,
    Subscriptions or Watch Later.
  * Turn on the new bell in a channel's subscribe button to get a system
    notification when it uploads a video, short, live stream or post. You can
    choose specific types per channel from the subscribe button's settings menu
    or in the subscription settings.
  * Sort your subscriptions into groups to filter the feed and channel list, and
    arrange channels in a custom order with drag and drop
  * Connect your own Yattee server in Settings → Advanced to load videos,
    channels, and search results from it and stream videos through it
  * Desktop: Use Custom Title Bar in Theme settings replaces the system title
    bar with the tab bar, or with the top navigation when tabs are elsewhere,
    and keeps the window controls in its corner styled for Windows, macOS,
    Plasma or GNOME

  [ More improvements ]
  * Choose whether new videos go to the top or bottom of each playlist's custom
    order from Edit Playlist Info.
  * Android builds now target Android 17 and request Nearby devices permission
    for local network connections.
  * Search keyboard shortcuts by action, section, or key combination.
  * Libraries are now stored in SQLite, so editing large playlists and histories
    saves much faster; your existing library moves over automatically and older
    versions can still open it
  * Arrange your playlists in a custom order with drag and drop, and reorder
    playlists and their videos with the arrow keys
  * Choose Full Width as the video or playlist view type to show one video per
    row, and use your Playlist View Type on phones too
  * Long playlists scroll more smoothly, and switching tabs is faster when many
    tabs are open
  * Releases now include signed build provenance, so you can check that a
    download was built by OpenTubeX's GitHub workflows with gh attestation
    verify --repo OpenTubeX/OpenTubeX
  * Subscription feeds show new videos while a large refresh is still running
    instead of waiting until it finishes
  * Android APKs are smaller, and new lite APKs of about 15 MiB leave out
    downloads and other yt-dlp features for devices with little storage
  * Swiping with the Bookmark gesture inside the bookmark playlist now removes
    the video from it
  * On Android, the app stays more responsive while it syncs and refreshes
    subscriptions after opening
  * Show a privacy warning when an Invidious fallback bypasses your instance and
    connects directly to YouTube.
  * Desktop users can schedule complete local backups to a chosen folder and
    limit how many backups are kept.
  * The desktop app uses about 55 MB less memory when the tray icon is enabled
    on Linux and Windows
  * Choose how many columns video and playlist grids show, or keep Auto to fit
    them to the window
  * History opens faster with a large watch history, and its channel filter
    loads channels as you scroll.
  * Boost quiet videos up to 200% volume from the player's settings menu after
    turning on Show Volume Boost Toggle in Playback settings
  * Pair a new device by scanning a code shown on a connected device, so a
    connected computer without a camera can add a phone
  * On Android, the app opens faster with a large library and stays responsive
    with many tabs open
  * Automatic downloads can wait until your device is charging, or on Android
    until it is on an unmetered network
  * When Settings or Downloads is moved to the app header, its window now opens
    out of and closes back into its header button
  * On Android, the predictive back gesture now previews going back through
    pages, dropdowns, context menus, the search bar, the Tab Organizer and the
    side navigation
  * Pin playlists and channels to the side navigation, or the More menu on
    phones, to open them from any page
  * On Android, closed-app subscription refreshes skip channels without new
    content, so the app has less to import when you open it
  * Hide the swipe-to-seek popup with the new "Show swipe-to-seek preview"
    option in Playback settings while keeping the seek-bar feedback.
  * Fullscreen panels now open as full-width, draggable bottom panels in
    portrait, including the queue during offline audio playback.
  * Downloads now use compact rows with visible thumbnails, an actions menu, and
    full file information in Details.
  * Swipe again to reverse queue, Play Next, fully watched, and download
    actions. These shortcuts also work in Downloads.
  * Choose Google Sans as a bundled app font in Appearance settings.
  * Show a second caption track at the same time as the main captions, and keep
    the auto-translation picked in the player for later videos
  * Watching external media now counts towards your watch statistics
  * Save the watch queue to a new or existing playlist, and add a whole playlist
    to the end of the queue from its playlist page.
  * Dragging a tab to either end of a tab bar with a scrollbar now scrolls the
    tab bar, so you can drop the tab next to tabs that were out of view.
  * Import per-channel playback speeds from the Youtube Speed By Channel
    userscript under Settings → Data & Storage → Advanced.
  * Video cards now show the channel name on its own line, with the view count
    and upload date below it, each marked with an icon.
  * Quick settings can now include 32 more settings, such as Hide Video Views,
    Hide Live Streams, Reduced Motion, Toast Position, Loop Shorts and Remember
    Volume
  * Choose a preferred video codec in Advanced settings, and switch between a
    video's codecs in the quality menu for either playback engine.
  * Playlist pages now label their main actions and group the rest in a More
    menu. Custom quick bookmark icons also show in playlist menus instead of a
    plain circle.
  * Turn on Enable Seek History in Playback settings to get back to where you
    were after a misclicked seek. The player menu lists the positions you jumped
    away from, and Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Shift+Z step back and forward through them.
  * Exporting and importing large backups no longer freezes the window, and
    videos open sooner when the pointer rests on them before the click
  * Settings and Downloads open, close, minimize and restore smoothly on slower
    systems and while the app is busy
  * On Android, Settings → Playback → Quality Limit on Metered Networks makes
    videos start at a lower quality on mobile data and other metered networks
  * The app opens, refreshes subscriptions, loads channels and switches between
    videos faster
  * The buttons below the video are now grouped into one toolbar, with a labeled
    Download button that shrinks to an icon when space is tight
  * Brightness, volume and playback speed swipes now show only their indicator
    instead of revealing the player controls
  * Turn on diagnostic logging in Settings > Advanced > Diagnostics to copy or
    save a report for bug reports, with cookies, tokens, IP addresses and URL
    parameters removed
  * Downloaded videos now show a badge on their thumbnails, and opening one
    plays the downloaded file instead of streaming it.
  * Pinned tabs show their pin as a small badge on the tab icon, which leaves
    more room for the title
  * Settings → Playback → Channel Settings now has one switch that turns channel
    playback settings on or off instead of one per setting. The other switches
    save changes automatically.
  * Load a local SRT or WebVTT subtitle file for a video from the captions menu
  * Set a playlist to shuffle by default from Edit Playlist Info, so it plays in
    random order from a random first video.
  * Leaving a video or switching to another tab now shrinks the video into the
    mini player with the same animation as scrolling past it.
  * Video cards now mark music videos with a music note, and music videos opened
    from lists, the queue or autoplay start at normal speed
  * Each playlist now remembers its own sort order, and encrypted sync carries
    it to your other devices.

  [ Fixed bugs ]
  * Fixed the missing OpenTubeX app icon on macOS.
  * Clearing a channel search right after submitting it no longer reloads the
    channel and resets its sort order.
  * Fixed the oversized tray icon in the macOS menu bar.
  * Made quick Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab switches skip menu rendering and
    preview loading. Holding Control still opens the tab switcher.
  * Resume at the current playback position when opening a video tab on another
    device, even before watch history syncs.
  * Fix clipped page previews while swiping into the mobile tab organizer and
    animate opening it by tapping its button.
  * Tap the mobile audio player to hide or show its controls.
  * Fixed stuck channel search spinners, repeated watched-history writes, stale
    sync history paging and cached image errors, and made comment filtering, tab
    updates and yt-dlp playback start faster.
  * Enabled toggles, such as the settings header buttons with Dynamic colors, no
    longer look the same as tapped, hovered or focused ones
  * Fixed the large gap below the search field on playlist pages in narrow
    windows
  * OpenTubeX unloads inactive tabs before memory runs out and reloads crashed
    windows. Advanced settings lets you disable automatic unloading or adjust
    its memory threshold and unload percentage. Automatically unloaded tabs show
    a memory badge.
  * Tapping the mobile mini player opens the video on the first tap, and short
    flicks now minimize or restore it
  * Overlapping SponsorBlock segments now show one skip notice with a shield for
    each skipped category, and Unskip plays the whole range instead of skipping
    part of it again
  * Search filters work on Android again
  * Restored rounded corners on the watch page cards on phones.
  * Material Black now keeps cards, bars, menus and search fields black instead
    of tinting them with the wallpaper color
  * Auto-generated subtitles get one rounded background per line instead of one
    per word
  * yt-dlp playback and downloads on desktop now solve YouTube's JavaScript
    challenges without a separate Deno installation
  * History sync no longer fails with "You cannot change a document's _id", and
    duplicate history entries for the same video are cleaned up
  * Pasted YouTube search links open again, YouTube playlists show their first
    videos while the rest load, channel links no longer pull you back after
    navigating away, the download list survives crashes, and hidden Android apps
    stop syncing in the background
  * A wide scrollbar no longer blocks clicks on buttons beside it. It stays thin
    until you point at it
  * History search results no longer flash a loading spinner when sync or a
    subscription refresh updates your history
  * Videos with AI-dubbed audio now default to captions in the original language
    instead of a transcript of a dub, and caption translations now translate
    from the original language
  * External media tabs keep their title when you reopen the same URL.
  * Fixed excess empty scrolling space below video details on Android, including
    when recommended videos are hidden or playback is offline.
  * Fixed the darkened thumbnail end screen sometimes failing to appear after
    seeking to the end of a paused video.
  * On Android, swiping down now exits fullscreen entered by rotating the
    device, including when "Ignore system rotation lock for fullscreen" is
    enabled.
  * Restore clickable donor handles in live chat donation messages.
  * Show playback speed controls for rewindable livestreams and premieres.
  * A fullscreen actions dock with a single action now centers its button
    instead of leaving extra space on one side
  * Shorts now show the subscription settings and notification bell next to the
    subscribe button, including in fullscreen.
  * Dragging in the Material accent color picker no longer lags
  * Fullscreen swipe and double-tap gestures stay on the video when the queue or
    another panel is open, and the fullscreen queue header fits on one row.
  * System media controls show the title and thumbnail of external media instead
    of the previously watched video.
  * Inactive tabs no longer blend into the tab bar in Black, Dark, Hot Pink,
    Dynamic colors, the Material themes and a few other themes
  * Changing the resolution of a video in legacy formats no longer starts it
    while paused, or pauses it when Start Videos Automatically is off
  * Expanding the mini player back to its video no longer briefly shows the
    previous page or its sidebar around the player.
  * Updated Electron so the desktop app no longer trusts the compromised eMudhra
    intermediate certificates
  * Menus opened from the ⋮ button on playlist cards now have touch-sized rows
    on phones and tablets.
  * Expanding the mini player back to its video keeps the player's rounded
    corners instead of briefly showing black corners.
  * Loading more Home recommendations adds the new videos to the end of the feed
    instead of reordering the videos already shown
  * The SponsorBlock submission panel's scrollbar now sits at the panel edge
    instead of covering the segment fields.
  * Page titles on Home, Subscriptions, Playlists, History and the other main
    pages now stay in the same place when you switch pages, and the
    Subscriptions title no longer crowds the feed tabs on phones
  * Closing the last window no longer stops background subscription refreshes
    when the close confirmation is turned off; OpenTubeX hides to the tray
    instead
  * On Android and iOS, quick settings and the onboarding tutorial now tell you
    to tap and hold the profile icon to switch profiles instead of
    right-clicking it.
  * Chapters open beside the video like the transcript and SponsorBlock, instead
    of switching to theatre mode when it is the default viewing mode
  * The player shows the video's thumbnail again while the video plays in
    Picture-in-Picture

 -- OpenTubeX contributors <info@opentubex.org>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:29:18 +0000
